      "page": 1,
      "text": "HT-8\nEightballers\nCDR D. Burkett NAS WHITING FIELD, FL CDR S. Kohl\nCommanding Officer Executive Officer\nTraining the World's Best Helicopter Pilots\nSaturday, 07-Nov-2026\nSUNRISE: 06:08 MOONRISE: 04:35 % ILLUM: 4% JULIAN DATE: 6311\nSUNSET: 16:55 MOONSET: 15:45\nTOTAL FLY EVENTS: 4 TOTAL FLY HRS: 8.0\nTOTAL SIM EVENTS: 10 TOTAL SIM HRS: 15.0\nQuestions:\nEP Question: AUTOROTATIVE LANDING\nGeneral: What are the crew rest requirements for staff and students?\nNATOPS: What is the diameter of the tail rotor blades?\nSOP: RADALTs shall be set no lower than ____ feet AGL during enroute portions of all VFR night flights.\nDUTY/WATCH ASSIGNED SIGN IN SIGN OUT\nFDO LT HUNG C 0700 0659\nDUTY DRIVER 1stLt NOFFSINGER B 0730 0729\nAM SDO LTJG MORRIS C 0700 1900\nPM SDO ENS GERHARDT T 1900 0700\n***** Notes *****\nSouth Field CTO 0700-2300\nPace CLOSED\n***** Upcoming Events *****\nSpencer CLOSED\nSanta Rosa CLOSED\nVETERAN\u2019S DAY \u2013 11 NOV\nHarold CLOSED\nSAU CHANGE OF COMMAND \u2013 12 NOV\nSite X CLOSED\nChoctaw CLOSED\nSTANDING NOTES:\n1. Snivels shall be in T-SHARP NLT 0800, two working days prior to the date of the snivel. Late snivels require a T-SHARP\nentry followed by verbal notification to the Operations Duty Officer. Late snivels will be handled on a case-by-case basis.\n2. All CAIs and MIL Classes are accessed via T-SHARP: https://tsharp.navsea.cloud.navy.mil . Students are responsible for\nensuring all prerequisite CAIs are completed prior to scheduled events.\n3. All are highly encouraged to complete SAFREP if a notable event occurs: https://saferep.safety.af.mil/\n4. Access publications via Eightball University: https://www.cnatra.navy.mil/tw5/ht8/university.asp or the HT-8 Sharepoint:\nhttps://flankspeed.sharepoint-mil.us/sites/HT-8Main/SitePages/HT8Home.aspx"
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "text": "SAFETY OFFICER OPERATIONS OFFICER EXECUTIVE OFFICER COMMANDING OFFICER\nD. MirandaHidalgo, Maj, USMC M. Dominik, LCDR, USNR S. Kohl, CDR, USN D. Burkett, CDR, USN\nFlight (Flight Event) Schedule\nLINE BRIEF SCHD SCHD LNCH LAND INSTRUCTOR STUDENT TYPE SCHD REMARKS\nNUM TIME T/O LAND ICAO ICAO EVENT FLT\nTIME\nT10-1 0700 0830 1030 KNDZ KNDZ Maj CHALFANT B LT BARROWCLOUGH FORM, QIP- 2.0 AIRSHOW AIRCRAFT; DIV\nM Concurrent LEAD W/ GATES,\nACHESINSKI, SCINTO\nT14-1 0700 0830 1030 KNDZ KNDZ Capt GATES L LT BOTTERBRODT G FORM, QIP- 2.0 AIRSHOW AIRCRAFT; FORM\nConcurrent W/ CHALFANT, ACHESINSKI,\nSCINTO\nT18-1 0700 0845 1045 KNDZ KNDZ LT ACHESINSKI J LT OPIZZO M FORM, QIP- 2.0 AIRSHOW AIRCRAFT; FORM\nConcurrent W/ CHALFANT, GATES,\nSCINTO\nT22-1 0700 0845 1045 KNDZ KNDZ Maj SCINTO K Capt ZLOGAR A FORM, QIP- 2.0 AIRSHOW AIRCRAFT; FORM\nConcurrent W/ CHALFANT, GATES,\nACHESINSKI\nSimulator (Sim Event) Schedule\nLINE BRIEF SCHD SIM/ INSTRUCTOR STUDENT TYPE SCHD REMARKS\nDEVICE\nNUM TIME T/O EVENT TIME\nL7U3-2 0700 0730 L7U3 CIV ASHFORD R 1stLt MARTIN C TRF3001R 1.5\nL7U5-2 0700 0730 L7U5 CIV ARMSTRONG W LTJG BOBREK E TRF3001A 1.5\nL7U6-3 0830 0900 L7U6 CIV DIDIER D 1stLt ASHBY L DAY3001A 1.5 OPT W/U\nLCDR REGIS M\nL6U3-3 0830 0900 L6U3 CIV LOEB J LTJG HARTNETT K DAY2003A 1.5\nL7U1-4 1000 1030 L7U1 CIV HASKINS P LTJG DURMUS K DAY3202A 1.5\nL7U6-4 0830 1030 L7U6 CIV COUREY J LTJG HEBL R DAY3001A 1.5 OPT W/U\nLCDR REGIS M\nL7U9-5 1130 1200 L7U9 CIV DIDIER D LTJG WEAVER T DAY3401A 1.5\nL7U3-6 1300 1330 L7U3 CIV ASHFORD R 1stLt TRULL B SAR3001A 1.5"
